# Merge to main needs permission and CMPH work

**No auto-merge.** Green tests, a feature-branch push, or “it is ready” are not permission.

**Do not merge to `main` until both:**

1. **CMPH work is done** (or executing this turn). Full list: [wrap-on-command.mdc](wrap-on-command.mdc).
2. **Permission this conversation** — **CMPH**, **CMPHD**, WRAP, “land it”, “merge to main”, “ship to main”, or “check in and merge”.

After they grant (2), do not ask “merge to main?” again. Still finish (1) before the merge.

Agents **may** commit and **may** `git push -u origin <feature-branch>` after the merge-ready gate **without** merging.

## What counts as CMPH permission

Any of these in this conversation, for the **current** ship:

- **CMPH** / **CMPHD** / WRAP / “land it” / “merge to main” / “ship to main” / “check in and merge”
- **CMPHD** = the same land as **CMPH**, then delete local and remote. **CMPH** (no **D**) never deletes.

**UCPH** is not merge permission. It is the feature branch only.

That permission authorizes the short land. It does **not** authorize SWAT unless this is the epic’s last in-scope story. **“Check in and merge”** on that last story checks in the story and closes the epic in the same turn ([epic-close.mdc](epic-close.mdc)).

Docs-only and rules-only slices have no human runtime check. Do not invent one. Ships that change what the user runs still need a human **PASS** (or an explicit waive) before that merge ([human-check.mdc](human-check.mdc)).

## Forbidden unless both gates are true

- `git checkout main` plus a merge or rebase of the story
- `git push origin main` (or any push that updates `main`)
- Deleting the feature branch as if it were already merged
- Opening a pull request unless the user asked for one
- Merging because the CMPH *work* is done but they never gave permission
- Merging because they said CMPH but skipping the CMPH *work*

## After both gates

Follow AGENT_HANDOFF → *Git workflow*: merge locally to `main`, push `origin main`. **Keep** the feature branch unless they typed **CMPHD**. Record the land sha in `doc/PROJECT_STATUS.md`. See [doc/git/Feature_Branch_Archaeology.md](../../doc/git/Feature_Branch_Archaeology.md).
